  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607196500: Typed bounded variable PostgreSQL parameters

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

Prepared statements may declare up to sixteen PostgreSQL parameter type OIDs
through `pg_prepare_typed`. `pg_execute_params` accepts a bounded Bind fragment
in a memory range independent from statement SQL. The `.kotoba` provider
revalidates format count and codes, parameter count, every signed length,
NULL representation, per-value and aggregate limits, text NUL exclusion,
result format count and exact buffer exhaustion before any transport write.

Text and binary values are supported per parameter. NULL is represented only
by PostgreSQL's four-byte `-1` length. The consumer cannot use the fragment to
select a statement, portal, result format, endpoint or arbitrary frontend
message; the provider supplies those fields and emits one Bind, Execute and
Sync sequence on the existing affine channel.

## Evidence

Released PostgreSQL 14.19 qualification declares three `int4` OIDs and executes
one text value, one NULL and one binary int4 value, obtaining `42`. It then
requires `22P02` for SQL-looking text supplied as a parameter, successfully
reuses the statement with text values and closes it. Malformed counts, unknown
formats, truncation, oversized values and mismatched OID lists fail closed.

This closes variable-count, NULL, binary-format and explicit-OID support for
the bounded prepared-statement slice. Portals/cursors, batching/pipelining,
COPY, pooling, rotation, compatibility matrices and soak remain open."}]
